# Root-level .dockerignore — applies only to services whose docker-compose
# build context is the repo root: intake-service and eligibility-service
# (adr/0005-eligibility-agent-runtime-and-resilience.md), records-service
# (Stage 3 — imports libs.patient_view_agent), and now gateway (it must copy
# config/roles.yaml, the live RBAC permission source, which lives outside its
# own directory). scheduling-service, interop-service and roi-service still
# build from their own directories with their own local .dockerignore.
#
# Note the consequence of gateway joining this list: `services/gateway/` can no
# longer be excluded here, so it is present in the other root-context services'
# build contexts too. That costs a few KB of context and nothing else — their
# Dockerfiles only COPY the paths they name.
.git/
.github/
frontend/
node_modules/
docs/
adr/
tests/
.claude/
.codex_tmp/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store

# Sibling services that still build from their own directories, so they are
# never needed in a root-context build. `services/gateway/` is deliberately
# NOT in this list any more — gateway now builds from the repo root.
services/scheduling-service/
services/interop-service/
services/roi-service/

# db/ is mounted into the Postgres container at runtime (docker-compose.yml);
# it is not part of any Python service's build.
#
# w8-planner-2 P2 (adr/0012), review round 1 fix (B1): ONE exception —
# intake-service's Dockerfile now COPYs the PHI backfill script
# (db/migrations/scripts/encrypt_existing_phi.py) so `make up`/`make seed`
# can run it via `docker compose exec`. The negation is listed at every
# parent level; a bare `!db/migrations/scripts/encrypt_existing_phi.py`
# alone does not re-include a file whose ancestor directory was already
# excluded.
db/
!db/migrations/
!db/migrations/scripts/
!db/migrations/scripts/encrypt_existing_phi.py
